<title>HONG KONG: HK GDP rises 4.3 pct in 2nd quarter of 1996.</title>
<headline>HK GDP rises 4.3 pct in 2nd quarter of 1996.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Census and Statistics Department gave the following estimates of real gross domestic product growth (in percent).</p>
<p>				 2nd qtr '96  1st qtr '96 (revised)</p>
<p> GDP			     4.3	    3.3</p>
<p>Components</p>
<p>Private consumption</p>
<p> expenditure:		  2.5	    3.4</p>
<p>Government consumption</p>
<p> expenditure:		  5.2	    2.9</p>
<p>				 2nd qtr '96  1st qtr '96 (revised)</p>
<p>Gross domestic fixed</p>
<p> capital formation:	 10.4	   11.5</p>
<p> Domestic exports:	  -9.0	   -7.4</p>
<p> Re-exports:		   6.5	    7.5</p>
<p> Exports of services:	5.2	    9.5</p>
<p>Implicit price</p>
<p> deflator of GDP:	    6.5	    6.0</p>
<p>Estimates of individual expenditure components of GDP for the 2nd quarter of 1996 were updated based on the latest data available from various sources, the government said.  </p>
<p>The following table is of revised GDP data. All figures are year-on-year at constant (1990) market prices.</p>
<p>				 1996 Q1   1995 Q4   1995 Q3   1995 Q2</p>
<p> GDP			     3.3	 3.5	 4.6	 5.2</p>
<p>Components</p>
<p>Private consumption</p>
<p> expenditure:		  3.4	 0.4	 1.0	 1.2</p>
<p>Government consumption</p>
<p> expenditure:		  2.9	 5.3	 5.8	 2.7</p>
<p>				 1996 Q1   1995 Q4   1995 Q3   1995 Q2</p>
<p>Gross domestic fixed</p>
<p> capital formation:	 11.5	 3.9	14.5	8.2</p>
<p> Total exports of goods    4.9	 6.8	12.2     12.7</p>
<p> Imports of goods	    5.2	 8.0	13.5     13.6</p>
<p> Exports of services	 9.5	10.0	12.8     12.4</p>
<p> Imports of services	 1.6	 4.4	 5.3	6.2</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
